      "created_at": "2013-05-18T13:48:04.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I forget the exact card (I don't own the box our group plays with), but the card in question reads something like, <em>\"Return all plating cards into your Hand.\"</em></p><p>Seems straightforward, except the wording allows the card to be interpreted as saying you may search your deck, discard, AND all cards in play for <em>every </em>plating card in Omnitron-X's deck and bring them into your hand immediately. My thinking, and the thinking of others in our group, is that it should probably read, \"...all plating cards <em><strong>In Play</strong></em>.\"</p><p>That way it handles like we interpret that it <em>should </em>play: you have to return all other plating cards that are currently in Play aside from that card, but you don't get to break the game in two by accelerating his Deck in a hax manner, which is to say, you perform multiple Search, Retrieve, and Return functions at the same time, without needing to reshuffle your Deck.</p><p>The way I've played him is that it's meant to read \"In Play\", therefore, I can only return cards that are in play before me, not all plating cards in the Discard since I have to Retrieve those, nor the Deck since I have to Draw or Search for them.</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:38:24.637Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
