      "raw": "<p>I forget the exact card (I don&#39;t own the box our group plays with), but the card in question reads something like, <em>&quot;Return all plating cards into your Hand.&quot;</em></p><p>Seems straightforward, except the wording allows the card to be interpreted as saying you may search your deck, discard, AND all cards in play for <em>every </em>plating card in Omnitron-X&#39;s deck and bring them into your hand immediately. My thinking, and the thinking of others in our group, is that it should probably read, &quot;...all plating cards <em><strong>In Play</strong></em>.&quot;</p><p>That way it handles like we interpret that it <em>should </em>play: you have to return all other plating cards that are currently in Play aside from that card, but you don&#39;t get to break the game in two by accelerating his Deck in a hax manner, which is to say, you perform multiple Search, Retrieve, and Return functions at the same time, without needing to reshuffle your Deck.</p><p>The way I&#39;ve played him is that it&#39;s meant to read &quot;In Play&quot;, therefore, I can only return cards that are in play before me, not all plating cards in the Discard since I have to Retrieve those, nor the Deck since I have to Draw or Search for them.</p>",
